fail[3]: A customer served at once from the stock they start with, at minute 0.
fail[4]: The first customer is still waiting at the restock on minute 5, after their deadline of 4, so they leave. The second customer is served at 5, when the restock arrives.
fail[5]: The first customer is served at minute 5, the last minute of their patience. The second gives up at 4, before the restock on minute 5 can help.
fail[6]: Three thousand restocks and twelve thousand customers. Each event must be handled in time order, with the line kept in a deque rather than a list searched each minute.
edges:
- no stock and no patience leaves :: restock_line(stock, restocks, customers) == [-1] :: run(0, [], [[3, 1, 0]])
- stock on hand is served at once :: restock_line(stock, restocks, customers) == [0] :: run(2, [], [[0, 1, 5]])
